3f5e0627d235d1540497e52b8cd74b5d5077b0fd
2026-05-27
Issue 14: Designate note-taker from party member list

Files changed:
- ui/lib/state/app_state_notifier.dart: added String? _noteTaker field;
  String? get noteTaker; void setNoteTaker(String? name) with unchanged-guard
  pattern consistent with setSelectedModel / setTemperature
- ui/lib/widgets/party_member_input.dart: replaced plain Text(name) list
  items with RadioListTile<String>; value=name, groupValue=noteTaker,
  onChanged delegates to appState.setNoteTaker; title uses bold TextStyle
  when name == noteTaker, null otherwise; dense+zeroPadding to keep
  compact inline with the sidebar
- ui/test/state/app_state_notifier_test.dart: added noteTaker group with
  6 tests covering: null initially, set, notify, no-op on same value,
  clear with null, replace previous
- ui/test/widgets/party_member_input_test.dart: added 5 note-taker widget
  tests covering: RadioListTile present per member, tap designates note-taker,
  selecting new replaces old, note-taker shown in bold, non-note-taker not bold
- user-stories/done/14-designate-note-taker.md: issue complete

Key decisions:
- RadioListTile<String> chosen over bare Radio<String> — single widget
  carries both the radio control and the label, reducing boilerplate and
  making find.widgetWithText(RadioListTile<String>, name) straightforward
  in tests
- Bold style applied only via the title Text style (not via ListTile
  selected colour) so the visual distinction is textual and doesn't
  conflict with the Radio's own selected-state rendering
- setNoteTaker lives in AppStateNotifier (single source of truth) and
  accepts null to allow future deselection; the widget never calls it
  with null because RadioListTile only fires onChanged with the value,
  not null

All 108 Flutter tests pass; flutter build windows --debug succeeds.

