  TextEditingController; Row with Expanded TextField + ElevatedButton(Add);
  _submit() delegates to appState.addPartyMember then clears controller when
  the trimmed name was non-empty; ListenableBuilder renders current partyMembers
  as Text widgets below the input
- ui/lib/widgets/main_shell.dart: imported party_member_input.dart; added
  PartyMemberInput to _buildSidebarChild Column on Q&A page (index 0), below
  TemperatureSlider with a 12px SizedBox gap
- ui/test/state/app_state_notifier_test.dart: added partyMembers group with
  6 tests covering: empty initially, append, notify, ignore empty, ignore
  whitespace, trim, multiple members
- ui/test/widgets/party_member_input_test.dart: new; 9 widget tests covering:
  TextField present, Add button present, tap Add adds to notifier, clears
  field, shows name in list, empty no-op, whitespace no-op, pre-existing
  members shown, list updates on notify
- ui/test/widgets/main_shell_test.dart: added import; 3 integration tests:
  PartyMemberInput visible on Q&A, absent on Summary, absent on Note Editor
- user-stories/done/13-add-party-member.md: issue complete

Key decisions:
- PartyMemberInput is StatefulWidget (owns TextEditingController) while
  list display is driven by ListenableBuilder on AppStateNotifier — no local
  list state needed
- addPartyMember no-op guard lives in AppStateNotifier (single source of truth
  for list validity), not in the widget
- Widget placed on Q&A page only (index 0), consistent with model selector and
  temperature slider placement

