bd3205f96e994f22a115a0408de5472db358a95b
2026-05-27
Issue 12: Model + temperature persistence to user_data.json

Files changed:
- ui/lib/services/user_preferences_service.dart: new UserPreferences value
  class and UserPreferencesService; load() reads user_data.json and returns
  defaults when file is absent or malformed; save() writes model (omitted
  when null) and temperature as JSON; return type Future<void> with synchronous
  writeAsStringSync so callers can await without needing runAsync
- ui/lib/state/app_state_notifier.dart: added prefsService optional param;
  _persist() fire-and-forgets save after setSelectedModel / setTemperature;
  added initialModel / initialTemperature constructor params so main() can
  pass loaded values in
- ui/lib/widgets/main_shell.dart: accepts optional UserPreferencesService;
  initState adds _savePreferences listener when service provided; also calls
  _applyStoredPreferences() to hydrate AppStateNotifier from disk on startup;
  dispose removes listener
- ui/lib/main.dart: loads UserPreferencesService and awaits initial prefs
  before runApp; passes prefsService and initialPrefs to TTRPGChatbotApp;
  TTRPGChatbotApp initializes AppStateNotifier with loaded model/temperature
- ui/test/services/user_preferences_service_test.dart: new; 10 unit tests
  covering load defaults, stored model, stored temperature, missing keys,
  malformed JSON, and round-trip saves for model+temperature, null model,
  and boundary values 0.0 / 1.0
- ui/test/state/app_state_notifier_test.dart: added initialisation-from-prefs
  group (3 tests) and persistence group (5 tests) using _FakePrefsService;
  covers model+temperature saved, no-op guards, combined snapshot
- ui/test/widgets/main_shell_test.dart: added _FakePrefsService helper class;
  replaced runAsync+pumpWidget file-I/O tests with fake-service variants to
  avoid runAsync/pumpWidget deadlock; 2 new integration tests: loads saved
  temperature on startup; saves preferences when AppStateNotifier changes
- user-stories/done/12-model-temperature-persistence.md: issue complete

Key decisions:
- save() uses writeAsStringSync (not writeAsString) so the Future<void>
  return resolves synchronously; this lets tests assert the saved state
  immediately after a state change without needing runAsync
- Persistence tests in main_shell_test use _FakePrefsService (in-memory) to
  avoid the Flutter test runAsync+pumpWidget deadlock that arises when real
  file I/O is started inside initState during pumpWidget
- _applyStoredPreferences() is kept in MainShell so the widget is
  self-contained for testing; in production main() also initializes
  AppStateNotifier from prefs before widget creation (harmless double-apply
  with no-op guards)

All 78 Flutter tests pass; flutter build windows --debug succeeds.

